@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] yorimichi-v2-targeted-authoring
A normal V2 build or play MUST NOT prepare, generate, import, resave or cook content. It validates, compiles
and checks committed packages. Preparation and import run only when explicitly asked, for the selected assets
and their declared dependents, through each asset's recorded route. An unchanged input MUST NOT launch Blender
or an Unreal import, and a no-op run MUST NOT rewrite any tracked file. Missing or stale content MUST fail with
the exact problem and its owner route, never be fixed silently, stamped as current or regenerated wholesale.
External and AI-generated sources are committed, pinned inputs recorded through atelier.ai.ledger.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] yorimichi-v2-single-writer
Every committed V2 package MUST have exactly one owning record: an asset's asset.toml output or a region's
actors.verified.json. Only that owner's route writes it: a generated package only through its importer, an
editor-owned package only through a claimed editor save and its save validation. A protected write MUST hold
an active claim covering the package's scope and exact path, and the LFS lock that claim recorded, verified
when the write is authorized; a task's changed-file set MUST stay inside its claim, including companions,
deletions and moves between regions. The only exception is DECISIONS D04: until D04 is closed, the recorded
bootstrap writer, in a checkout with no claims task, is the single binary writer and writes without a claim.
One creation exception: World Partition names a new actor package only when it saves it, so a migration whose
active claim holds every touched region's scope MAY create new packages in those regions' actor folders before
their paths are claimed; it MUST then bind each to the claim with its acquired LFS lock and verify them before
publication. A refused bind MUST delete every file it created. When the claim service itself fails (unreachable,
timed out, unsettled, remote unavailable) after the created files passed their own checks, they MUST all move out
of the content tree (build/yorimichi_v2/migrate/pending) for a resumed bind, which re-checks them first and follows
the same rule; no new migration runs while they wait. Existing files stay exact-claimed.
Every write route (import, editor script, save validation, adoption) MUST enforce the same rule, and adoption
MUST NOT overwrite an existing package whose bytes differ.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:security] yorimichi-v2-portable-records
Asset, region and verification records MUST be portable: repository-relative paths, hashes, engine identity
and versions only, never absolute paths, hostnames, user names or times used as evidence. Package bytes
committed to Git LFS MUST NOT carry absolute donor or home paths in their import metadata; the repository is
public and LFS is not private storage. Asset licenses and redistribution rights MUST be settled before bytes
are uploaded.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] yorimichi-v2-joins-checked
Editor-authored joins between saved actors (stairs, paving, decks, region borders) MUST be accepted by an
automated gap and overlap check over the saved actors, in addition to the inherited ground, seam, closure and
walkability rules.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:architecture] yorimichi-v2-excluded-features
V2 MUST NOT load, register or link phone streaming (PixelStreaming2, AtelierStream, touch pages) or go-kart
driving (the Driving plugin, kart assets, kart UI). Shared input, audio, menu and travel code stays when an
included feature uses it; an excluded dependency is removed cleanly, leaving no missing class, asset load or
dead menu entry. V2 runtime code MUST NOT import or load files from games/yorimichi.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] yorimichi-v2-warm-editor-jobs
One warm editor MAY run several editor jobs (tools/editor/session.py, step editor.session) only when each job is
authorized immediately before it runs, under its own claim and with its own save lists, by the same code as the
job's cold step. Object and editor-script jobs MUST use that step's checking code before the next job starts.
Import jobs MUST verify their own written files and expected packages before the next job; these receipts are
provisional. The importing caller MUST perform final import validation and record acceptance after the editor exits.
Between jobs the editor MUST refuse
every save. A job that fails or leaves a package unsaved MUST end the session. The session MUST end when its
editor scripts or C++ change, and every file it wrote MUST be one a job's own check accepted. The build's lock,
admission and memory guard own the session's whole life; only its controller writes its checkout.
An explicitly headless session MAY share capacity with another checkout. Both its controller and its editor
MUST reject every job except object migration and prepared static-mesh imports; textures, arbitrary scripts and
captures retain rendered sessions. An import job MUST use the cold import authorization and verify its own writes
before the next job. The importing caller owns journals and final records; recovery MUST wait for the editor to end.
Shared sessions MUST still hold disjoint claims, including region and environment companion packages.
